JH <no@email> wrote:
> Shouldn't one be able to dip a towel in water, and then wield it as a (more
> powerful than a dry towel) weapon?  (or is this already implemented... I
> didn't see anything that mentions it).

    I am pretty sure it's not implemented.  Towels are of type TOOL,
but any tool that can be used as a weapon is type WEPTOOL.  That would
be pretty simple to fix: just make a towel WEPTOOL with hit type WHACK.
The wetting part might be a little more difficult, since "wet" is not
an attribute something can currently have.  Two ways I can think of to
do it are: 1. add the new attribute, 2. have two types of objects, 
"towel" and "wet towel", the first being of type TOOL and the second of
type WEPTOOL, and the first turns into the second when you dip it in 
water.

	Of course, then you have to start thinking about other questions,
like, What happens when you fall in the water?  Does your towel 
automatically become a wet towel?  What if you get hit by a fire trap?
Will your towel dry out again?  Should it dry out on its own?  If you
can whap a troll with a wet towel, can you also give him a wedgie?


